Since $\overline {a}=(2, -1, 3)$, $\overline {b}=(-1, 4, -2)$, and $\overline {c}=(7, 5, \lambda)$ are coplanar vectors, the determinant formed by these vectors must be zero:

$$
\begin{vmatrix}
2 & -1 & 3 \\
-1 & 4 & -2 \\
7 & 5 & \lambda
\end{vmatrix} = 0
$$

Expanding the determinant, we have:

\begin{align*}
0 &= 2 \begin{vmatrix} 4 & -2 \\ 5 & \lambda \end{vmatrix} - (-1) \begin{vmatrix} -1 & -2 \\ 7 & \lambda \end{vmatrix} + 3 \begin{vmatrix} -1 & 4 \\ 7 & 5 \end{vmatrix} \\
&= 2(4\lambda - (-10)) - (-1)(-1\lambda - 14) + 3(-5 - 28) \\
&= 8\lambda + 20 + \lambda + 14 - 99 \\
&= 9\lambda - 65
\end{align*}

Setting this equal to zero and solving for $\lambda$ gives us:

$$
\lambda = \frac{65}{9}
$$

Substituting $\lambda$ back into $\overline {c}$, we obtain $\overrightarrow {c}=(7, 5, \frac{65}{9})$.

The projection of $\overline {c}$ onto $\overline {a}$ can be found by the formula:

$$
\text{Projection of } \overline {c} \text{ onto } \overline {a} = \frac{\overrightarrow {a} \cdot \overrightarrow {c}}{|\overrightarrow {a}|}
$$

Calculating the dot product $\overrightarrow {a} \cdot \overrightarrow {c}$ and the magnitude $|\overrightarrow {a}|$:

\begin{align*}
\overrightarrow {a} \cdot \overrightarrow {c} &= (2)(7) + (-1)(5) + (3)\left(\frac{65}{9}\right) \\
&= 14 - 5 + \frac{195}{9} \\
&= \frac{126+195}{9} \\
&= \frac{321}{9}
\end{align*}

\begin{align*}
|\overrightarrow {a}| &= \sqrt{(2)^2 + (-1)^2 + (3)^2} \\
&= \sqrt{4 + 1 + 9} \\
&= \sqrt{14}
\end{align*}

Now, using these values to find the projection:

$$
\text{Projection of } \overline {c} \text{ onto } \overline {a} = \frac{\frac{321}{9}}{\sqrt{14}} = \frac{321}{9\sqrt{14}}
$$

To rationalize the denominator, we multiply by $\frac{\sqrt{14}}{\sqrt{14}}$:

\begin{align*}
\text{Projection of } \overline {c} \text{ onto } \overline {a} &= \frac{321}{9\sqrt{14}} \cdot \frac{\sqrt{14}}{\sqrt{14}} \\
&= \frac{321\sqrt{14}}{9 \cdot 14} \\
&= \frac{321}{9 \cdot 2} \cdot \sqrt{14} \\
&= \frac{321\sqrt{14}}{18} \\
&= \frac{107\sqrt{14}}{6} \\
&= \boxed{\frac{107\sqrt{14}}{6}}
\end{align*}

